     {
          "algorithm": "The algorithm calculates an Adaptive Structural Fragility Index for each unvisited node by dynamically blending betweenness centrality and core number based on the graph's bridge ratio, then multiplying by eigenvector centrality and dividing by local clustering plus epsilon, selecting the node with the maximum score to prioritize both immediate bridge destruction and long-term core collapse while avoiding locally redundant targets.",
          "code": "def select_next_node(graph, unvisited_nodes):\n    bridge_ratio = graph.graph['precomputed']['bridge_ratio_high_bc']\n    best_node = None\n    best_score = -float('inf')\n    \n    for node in unvisited_nodes:\n        n = graph.nodes[node]\n        w_b = 0.5 + bridge_ratio\n        w_c = 1.5 - bridge_ratio\n        score = ((w_b * n['betweenness'] + w_c * n['core_number']) * \n                 n['eigenvector']) / (n['clustering'] + 1e-9)\n        if score > best_score:\n            best_score = score\n            best_node = node\n            \n    return best_node",
